# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=rogue:assassination style=melee size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=844x390,touch save=carried (behaves as fresh, #273 --
# carried never actually carries across separate playbot invocations because
# the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: rogue:assassination has crossed THE VIGIL
# clean twice under `melee`/`mash`, but only ever at 10-normal -- this is the
# first rogue:assassination evening at 25-heroic and the first `melee`-style
# evening at 25-heroic of any class. direction.md's #6 line has been
# narrowing toward "size/difficulty, not style" separating a clean VIGIL
# crossing from a stall (good/dodge/flee all crossed clean at 25-heroic where
# they, or others, stalled at 10-normal) -- this either adds a fourth style to
# that 25-heroic-clean pile on the one class that already crosses fast at
# 10-normal too, or breaks the pattern. `melee`'s own beeline-at-boss steering
# (no away-from-hazard term) also makes this a fresh read on whether a pure
# melee dps can survive Bonegrinder heroic's bonestorm aura (#267) at 25-man
# scale, where the only prior melee-vs-bonestorm data point is a 10-normal
# eight-wipe streak.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:rogue:assassination
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening melee 200 5
state
shot end
says
bill
